Hybrid cloud operations involve managing workloads that remain distributed between on-premises infrastructure and Azure. Organizations often use this model while gradually transitioning to the cloud or when certain workloads must remain on-premises.

Hybrid operations may involve:

* VPN Gateway
* ExpressRoute
* Azure Arc
* Identity synchronization
* DNS integration
* Shared monitoring
* Hybrid application architectures

For example, an organization may keep a sensitive database in its datacenter while hosting the application layer in Azure.

A real-life use case is a manufacturing company maintaining factory systems on-premises while using Azure for analytics and centralized application services.

Hybrid cloud operations provide flexibility while allowing organizations to modernize gradually.
